Z||000000||Philphine||02-13-2001||11:15 PM||||i stuck it in my sig but i haven't mentioned that i bought fierodaves's choptop fiero. bettween weather and work i haven't done much more than look at it out the window. sunday it was fairly warm and i had time to look it over a little. so far all i've done is cut the wing off. i also looked at the trunk area. dave said it didn't have a trunk but if you look under the car it's still there. i thought it had a panel riveted over it but it is actually some kind of security torx screws. some may have noticed my post about where to get bits for them. i got them today and when i get time again i'll try to get it open. <P>since it seems dave didn't open it there's no telling how long it's been sealed up. (eyes glaze over) maybe since '84. there's no telling whats in it. maybe superduty engine parts. or plans for the fiero engine that should have come with it. or hidden documents that prove the corvette faction killed the fiero. i'm sure it's something spectacular.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>i may try to get it broadcast as pay for view.<P>stay tuned...<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
